The benchmark values are one trial using the kernel's coarse global `uptime()` tick counter. They include only the user `write()` call, but tick resolution and QEMU scheduling are coarse; repeat trials and report spread before drawing performance conclusions. The concurrent-write check verifies the resulting file has the expected length and only bytes written by either child; it is a functional smoke test, not a formal atomicity guarantee.

